@startuml
!theme plain
title D05 solution status and revision type

state "Solution status (SolutionStatus), set once at insert" as S {
  [*] --> SUCCESS : callback / revision / Pareto apply,\nno order unassigned
  [*] --> PARTIAL_SUCCESS : callback / revision / Pareto apply,\nsome orders unassigned
  [*] --> INFEASIBLE : completion callback,\nno feasible plan
  state INITIAL #EEEEEE : declared in the enum,\nnever written by any code path
}

state "Revision chain (SolutionType)" as R {
  [*] --> ENGINE_GENERATED : completion callback\n(root of the chain)
  ENGINE_GENERATED --> MANUAL_EDITED : POST /solutions/{id}/revisions\nbase is latest, no hard violation
  ENGINE_GENERATED --> PARETO_ALTERNATIVE : POST /solutions/{id}/pareto/{cid}/apply\nFRONTIER candidate, same order set
  MANUAL_EDITED --> MANUAL_EDITED : save again on the latest revision
  MANUAL_EDITED --> PARETO_ALTERNATIVE : apply a candidate
  PARETO_ALTERNATIVE --> MANUAL_EDITED : edit the applied plan
  PARETO_ALTERNATIVE --> PARETO_ALTERNATIVE : apply another candidate
}

note bottom of R
  Every new revision is a new row (parent_solution_id = base);
  an existing row's status and type never change.
  A save or apply on a base that is not the latest revision is 409
  (RevisionConflictException carrying the latest id); nothing is written.
  FILE_IMPORTED exists in the enum; no code path creates it.
end note
@enduml
